<!--
  ⛔ A STIPULATION, NOT A FILING. Nothing here was measured. The figures exist to put one
  state of the model in front of a checker, and that state is a PARTIAL NAMEPLATE
  ELIMINATION: two parts that each hold their own capacity AND a block they both count.

  ⭐⭐ WHY THE CELL WAS DARK. Every sized nameplate elimination in this repository removes a
  WHOLE part's nameplate — one machine both members filed. That reads as "one supply, several
  claimants" and invites the conclusion that a nameplate elimination discriminates a KIND of
  fusion. It does not. `e` is a MAGNITUDE: how much supply the parts counted in common. Here it
  is 3 of a 10, which is neither none nor a whole part, and the arithmetic is unchanged.

    team-a nameplate   10 shifts per week   7 its own, plus the 3 it may call on
    team-b nameplate   10 shifts per week   7 its own, plus the SAME 3
    shared block        3 shifts per week   counted by both, so eliminated once
    fused              17 shifts per week   10 + 10 - 3

  ⭐ AND THE PARTS ARE FUNGIBLE THROUGHOUT, at e = 0, at e = 3 and at e = 10. Fungibility is a
  judgement carried in `observed`; the elimination is an adjustment to an arithmetic. They are
  independent axes, which is the reading this document exists to make unavailable.
-->
